{"event": "episode_start", "task_id": "med_01", "tier": "medium", "seed": 0, "model": "mock/solver", "system_prompt": "You are Gatekeeper, an autonomous access-policy repair agent inside a simulated company.\n\nYou are given a broken JSON access policy, a directory of users/groups/resources, and natural-language access requirements. Your job is to edit the policy so it matches the requirements exactly, then call submit.\n\nEvaluation semantics:\n- Default deny: a request is allowed only when an allow statement applies.\n- An explicit deny always overrides an allow.\n- Within a statement, the listed principals, actions and resources are alternatives. Every condition must match the request context.\n- Exceptions exempt those principals from that statement.\n- Statements are evaluated deterministically by id; the deciding deny is the first matching deny, otherwise the first matching allow.\n- The hidden check covers every user, action, resource and supported context variant, including names and context keys not mentioned in the requirements.\n\nSelector syntax:\n- Principal: \"user:<id>\", \"group:<id>\", or \"*\".\n- Resource: \"resource:<id>\", \"tag:<tag>\", or \"*\".\n- Action: \"read\", \"write\", \"delete\", \"share\", or \"*\".\n- Context: string keys such as \"network\" and \"mfa\"; a key may be absent.\n\nRules:\n- Do not execute shell commands; you have no shell. Use only the provided tools.\n- Do not guess: inspect groups, users, resources and visible examples with the tools.\n- You may call up to 10 tools in one reply and take up to 40 turns.\n- Work efficiently. When the policy matches the requirements, call submit.\n", "initial_observation": "Task med_01 (medium).\n\nAccess requirements for Gatekeeper task med_01 (medium).\n\nThe company uses the actions read, write, delete and share.\nA request is allowed only when an allow rule applies and no deny rule\napplies. An explicit deny always overrides an allow. Every condition\non a rule must match. Requests that no rule allows are denied by\ndefault. Within a rule, the listed principals, actions and resources\nare alternatives; they do not all need to match.\n\nGroups (members can be users or nested groups):\n- group g01: user u008, user u020, user u021, user u022, or user u029\n- group g02: user u005, user u011, user u017, user u018, user u019, user u026, user u027, or user u030\n- group g03: user u004, user u008, or user u009\n- group g04: user u001, user u010, or user u021\n- group g05: user u004, user u006, user u007, user u013, user u018, user u023, user u024, or user u025\n- group g06: user u007, user u009, user u015, or user u017\n- group g07: user u003, user u012, user u014, or user u015\n\nRules:\n1. Allow all users to any action all resources.\n2. Deny all users permission to any action resources tagged scope:restricted.\n3. Deny members of group g03 permission to share or delete resource r036 or resource r056 only when mfa is false.\n4. Deny members of group g02 permission to delete or read resource r022 or resource r020.\n5. Deny members of group g06 permission to share resource r045.\n6. Deny members of group g01 or members of group g02 permission to share resource r001, resource r032, or resources tagged project:cobalt only when mfa is true and network is vpn.\n7. Deny user u027 or user u001 permission to share resources tagged dept:eng or resource r001.\n8. Deny members of group g05 permission to delete resource r012 or resources tagged project:beacon. This rule does not apply to user u008 or user u017.\n9. Deny members of group g06 permission to read resources tagged dept:eng only when network is guest.\n10. Deny user u030 or user u028 permission to share or delete resource r041, resource r056, or resource r014.\n\nThe hidden check covers every user, action, resource and supported\ncontext variant. Some checked users, groups, resources and condition\nkeys are intentionally not mentioned above; inspect the directory\nrather than assuming the visible names are exhaustive.\n\nCurrent access policy (this policy is broken):\n{\n  \"statements\": [\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"*\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": null,\n      \"effect\": \"allow\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s001\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"*\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"*\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": null,\n      \"effect\": \"deny\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s002\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"*\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"tag:scope:restricted\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"share\",\n        \"delete\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": null,\n      \"effect\": \"deny\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s003\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"group:g03\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"resource:r036\",\n        \"resource:r056\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"delete\",\n        \"read\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": null,\n      \"effect\": \"allow\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s004\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"group:g02\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"resource:r022\",\n        \"resource:r020\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"share\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": null,\n      \"effect\": \"deny\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s005\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"group:g06\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"resource:r045\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"share\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": {\n        \"mfa\": \"true\",\n        \"network\": \"vpn\"\n      },\n      \"effect\": \"deny\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s006\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"group:g01\",\n        \"group:g02\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"resource:r001\",\n        \"resource:r032\",\n        \"tag:project:cobalt\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"share\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": null,\n      \"effect\": \"deny\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s007\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"user:u027\",\n        \"user:u001\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"tag:dept:eng\",\n        \"resource:r001\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"delete\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": null,\n      \"effect\": \"deny\",\n      \"exceptions\": [\n        \"user:u008\",\n        \"user:u017\"\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"s008\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"group:g05\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"resource:r012\",\n        \"tag:project:beacon\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"read\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": {\n        \"network\": \"guest\"\n      },\n      \"effect\": \"deny\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s009\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"group:g06\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"tag:dept:eng\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"share\",\n        \"delete\"\n      ],\n      \"condition\": null,\n      \"effect\": \"deny\",\n      \"exceptions\": [],\n      \"id\": \"s010\",\n      \"principals\": [\n        \"user:u030\",\n        \"user:u028\"\n      ],\n      \"resources\": [\n        \"resource:r041\",\n        \"resource:r056\",\n        \"resource:r014\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nTools: get_requirements, list_policies, lookup, simulate, put_policy, delete_policy, undo, diff, check_examples, submit. Call submit only when you believe the policy is repaired.", "initial_state_hash": "073c02ef", "append_text": "", "ts": "2026-10-23T22:33:29.459606+00:00"}
